# Database Access with Drizzle

All database reads and writes must go through the Drizzle schema defined in `src/schema.ts` and the Drizzle query builder. Raw SQL and direct database client calls are not allowed.

## Schema

Tables and inferred types live in `src/schema.ts`:
- `decksTable` — `InsertDeck` / `SelectDeck`
- `cardsTable` — `InsertCard` / `SelectCard`

Always import tables and types from `src/schema.ts`.

## Queries

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — raw SQL or direct client
const rows = await client.query("SELECT * FROM decks WHERE user_id = $1", [userId]);

// ✅ GOOD — Drizzle query builder
import { db } from "@/db";
import { decksTable } from "@/schema";
import { eq } from "drizzle-orm";

const decks = await db.select().from(decksTable).where(eq(decksTable.userId, userId));
```

## Mutations

```typescript
// ✅ INSERT
await db.insert(decksTable).values({ userId, title, description });

// ✅ UPDATE
await db.update(decksTable).set({ title }).where(eq(decksTable.id, id));

// ✅ DELETE
await db.delete(decksTable).where(eq(decksTable.id, id));
```

## Types

Use the inferred types for function signatures — do not redefine table shapes manually.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
function createDeck(deck: { userId: string; title: string }) {}

// ✅ GOOD
import { InsertDeck, SelectDeck } from "@/schema";
function createDeck(deck: InsertDeck) {}
```
